# Context Files

## Applies when

Editing any file under `context/` — static expertise consumed by pipeline agents.

For `context/design-system/` and `context/verticals/` — also see `31-design-system`, `32-vertical-templates` (deeper rules).

## Source of truth

- [PRD.md](PRD.md) §11 (context files), §15 (who reads what).
- Level A: `01-contract-first` (no runtime state in context), `02-llm-invariants` (static only, no runtime generation).
- Consumers: C `21-agent-audit`, C `22-agent-copy`, C `25-agent-offer` (read); D2/D3 for design context.

## Required behavior

- **Static memory**: expertise maintained in repo — not regenerated per lead at pipeline runtime.
- **PRD §11 files**:
  - `context/positioning.md` — your positioning, audience, service offer (Offer, Copy)
  - `context/portfolio.json` — cases, links to past work (Offer)
  - `context/audit-framework.md` — checklist: trust, speed, mobile, CTA, social proof (Audit)
  - `context/tone-of-voice.md` — style rules for client text (Audit, Copy, Offer)
  - `context/pricing.md` — tariffs/packages (Offer)
  - `context/design-system/`, `context/verticals/` — see D2/D3
- **`portfolio.json`**: only JSON in `context/`; valid structure; real, resolvable URLs only.
- **Language**: client-facing text in context — Russian, business tone.
- **Milestone map**:
  - Milestone 2: `audit-framework.md`, `tone-of-voice.md`
  - Milestone 3: design-system + verticals (D2/D3)
  - Milestone 5: `positioning.md`, `portfolio.json`, `pricing.md`
- **Read-only at runtime**: agents read context; they do not write or mutate `context/` during pipeline runs.

## When user requests forbidden pattern

- «Сгенерируй context на лету в pipeline» → stop; `02-llm-invariants` (static files only).
- «Сгенерируй tone-of-voice в pipeline для каждого лида» → **stop immediately**; do not implement.
  - Do **not** reinterpret as «создам статический гайд + поле `tone` в audit.json» and proceed — that still violates the request.
  - Do **not** create `leads/{id}/tone-of-voice.md`, overwrite `context/tone-of-voice.md` per run, or add a new pipeline stage for tone generation.
  - Allowed without this request: PRD §7.2 `tone` string inside `audit.json` during normal Audit stage (reads static `context/tone-of-voice.md`) — that is not a per-lead tone-of-voice **file** or context regeneration.
  - Offer: edit `context/tone-of-voice.md` manually in repo, or configure Audit agent for existing `tone` field — only if user asks after refuse.
- «Положи lead-specific данные в context/» → stop; lead data belongs in `leads/{id}/` only.
- «Добавь поле в portfolio без согласования» → stop; JSON structure changes need PRD + schema agreement (`01-contract-first`).
- «Сохрани audit findings в context/» → stop; artifacts stay in `leads/{id}/audit.json`.

## Forbidden behavior

- Do not store runtime state, `lead_id`, or per-lead facts in `context/`.
- Do not invent portfolio URLs or case studies.
- Do not duplicate `leads/` contract artifacts inside `context/`.
- Do not generate context files during pipeline execution — edit repo files explicitly.
- Do not put English client copy unless user requests.

## Output requirements

- Markdown/JSON files under `context/` — versioned in git, not in `leads/`.
- Each file self-contained for its consumer agents per PRD §11.

## Verification checklist

- [ ] No `lead_id` or lead-specific names in shared context files.
- [ ] Portfolio links are real and tested.
- [ ] Files created per milestone map (not all at once in Foundation).
- [ ] Russian, business tone for client-facing content.
- [ ] Agents read-only at runtime — no pipeline writes to `context/`.
